{"abstract":[{"text":"A seed for every decision, derived from a path, so adding a draw in one place never moves the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"numbers in another.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiftPRNG\/documentation\/SwiftPRNG\/UsingSeedTrees"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SeedTree"},{"text":" derives each node’s seed from its parent’s seed and a key, which is a name or an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"index. Each decision draws from its own node. Customer 7 arrives at the same time whether or not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"you add customer 6, and whether or not the code before it draws one more number.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let tree = SeedTree(42)","let arrival = tree[\"customer\", 7, \"arrival\"].uniform(in: 0 ..< 60)","var choices = tree[\"customer\", 7, \"choices\"].generator","let aisle = choices.integer(in: 0 ..< 12)","let arrivals = (0 ..< 3).map { customer in tree[\"customer\", customer, \"arrival\"].uniform(in: 0 ..< 60) }"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keys can be literals or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"String"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":" values."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A node’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"description"},{"type":"text","text":" gives its path and seed, as in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/customer\/7 (seed 1271…)"},{"type":"text","text":". Print it when a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"test fails."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To change one part of a tree, override a node: everything under i